<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Oh?\'92 Sarah found it difficult to find a comfortable way to sit on the sofa.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91They said you were only there a few minutes, until you whisked him away for a dinner date.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah hesitated momentarily, searching for what to say next. Hayley noticed; it should have been an easy segue from Agent Jones visiting Sarah to needing to warn Supaporn of the danger, though how an Airborne woman would care enough about a Cloudborne grunt she\'92d only met hours before \'85 in all her years of investigating crime Hayley had never met an Airborne of Sarah\'92s station (as evidenced by her undeniable attractiveness and therefore the quality of her lineage) who cared about anyone but themselves.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The dinner date was a cover to get Supaporn away from his friends so you could warn him that a PAPER agent was looking for him,\'92 Hayley prompted, to give Sarah another opportunity.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yes, that\'92s right,\'92 Sarah said, but it didn\'92t ring true to Hayley.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley looked away towards the garden, but observed Sarah in her peripheral vision. Sarah was breathing deeper than she was moments ago. There was something else going on here, so Hayley put her planned line of enquiry aside while she pursued another thread. \'91Tell me about Supaporn\'92s friends.\'92 Even from the corner of her eye, she could detect Sarah\'92s unblinking stare. When Hayley looked at her directly, for the first time since she\'92d sat down, Sarah aligned herself to projecting a calmer image for Hayley.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91There were three of them. I don\'92t recall their names; they were just barflies, the kind of drinking buddies you\'92d expect a cleaner to drink with.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley allowed silence to rest while she held Sarah\'92s gaze, which was as good as asking 
\f2\i all three of them
\f1\i0 ?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah held herself rigid for as long as she could endure.  \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Hey,\'92 Hayley offered, and put a friendly hand on Sarah\'92s knee. \'91What\'92s got you so spooked?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah shook her head. The she stared at Hayley, appraising her.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley gently massaged Sarah\'92s thigh. \'91You can trust me.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah processed her thoughts for several seconds while Hayley held her gaze and waited for something to shift. When the corner of Sarah\'92s mouth twitched, Hayley nodded and smiled. Sarah smiled a little too, and nodded momentarily in time with Hayley.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91One of them is an undercover agent of some kind \'85 PAPER, I thought \'85 I hope.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Hey, even if he\'92s police, I\'92m on your side, OK?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah nodded uncertainly and looked down at the rug under the coffee table.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Which of them did you suspect?\'92 Hayley asked, not risking revealing she already knew who it would be.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91His name is Halo.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Ah, the pick-up artist, Haloren Smythe.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You interviewed him?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I tried \'85\'92 Hayley hesitated while she weighed the impact of telling Sarah. \'91\'85 and nearly got my arse shot off by a PAPER gunship.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah exhaled and nodded herself to a more animated state. \'91I knew he was PAPER. It seemed like they\'92d got there before me, but Tony told me they\'92d been friends for years.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Interesting. What made you suspect him of being an undercover operative?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91He\'92s got empathy tech, and not just the consumer-grade stuff creepy philanthropists buy. His is the high-grade stuff only agencies have access to.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley wondered how Sarah would know that. \'91That\'92s very interesting.\'92 She was feeling both the triumph of reaffirming her theory that Halo was the Nightclub Vampire, and the frustration that she was imprisoned while he was roaming free. \'91Let\'92s return to Agent Jones. Why is he so sure you and Supaporn have stolen state secrets?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah went and stood at the doors to the front garden and placed her gaze out there somewhere, her back to Hayley. She hoped Hayley didn\'92t see her flinch as she relived the full force in a moment of Tony\'92s truck tipping on its side and careening into a food cart. She heard Johnny\'92s words in her head: 
